<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulysses S. Grant</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1822–1885</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odysseus">Ulysses</a> S. Grant was an American general and the 18th president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. As commander of the Union armies he defeated the Confederacy in the Civil War of 1861–1865, and as president from 1869 to 1877 he oversaw Reconstruction in the South. During a world tour in 1879 he offered his good offices to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in their dispute over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryukyu-islands">Ryukyu Islands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant.jpg" alt="Ulysses S. Grant" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Brady-Handy Photograph Collection, Library of Congress · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulysses_S._Grant_1870-1880_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
